.Dd April 19, 2026
.Dt PROWL-GENERATOR 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm prowl-generator
.Nd generate prowld unit files from rc.d scripts
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar rc.d_script
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a utility to help migrate legacy
.Xr rc.d 8
scripts to native
.Xr prowld 8
unit files.
It parses the header comments of a provided script and emits a
.Xr prowld 8
compatible JSON/UCL configuration to standard output.
.Pp
The generator extracts the following information from the script:
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Cm PROVIDE :
Used to derive the unit's
.Va rc_name
and primary capability.
.It
.Cm REQUIRE :
Mapped to
.Va requires
dependencies.
.It
.Cm BEFORE :
Mapped to
.Va before
dependencies.
.It
.Cm KEYWORD :
The
.Dq shutdown
keyword enables
.Va shutdown_wait
and the
.Dq nostart
keyword disables
.Va run_at_load
in the generated unit.
.El
.Pp
The resulting unit file is set to
.Va type :
.Cm oneshot
by default, as legacy scripts typically manage their own background processes.
The
.Va label
is automatically prefixed with
.Dq org.midnightbsd.rc.
to maintain consistency with the
.Xr prowld 8
rc-shim.
.Pp
The script must be an executable regular file owned by root and not
writable by group or other, and its basename must be usable in a unit
label (alphanumerics and
.Qq \&. ,
.Qq \&- ,
.Qq _ ,
.Qq @);
otherwise
.Nm
exits with an error.
.Pp
.Va run_at_load
is true only when the service is enabled: scripts with the
.Dq nostart
keyword never run at load, scripts without a
.Va rcvar=
assignment always do, and otherwise the rcvar (or
.Dq <PROVIDE>_enable )
must be
.Dq YES
in
.Pa /etc/defaults/rc.conf ,
.Pa /etc/rc.conf
or
.Pa /etc/rc.conf.local .
.Pp
Tokens longer than 255 characters and dependency lists longer than 32
entries are truncated, with a warning printed to standard error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Generate a unit file for the SSH daemon:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
prowl-generator /etc/rc.d/sshd > sshd.unit
.Ed
.Pp
Review the output for a local service:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
prowl-generator /usr/local/etc/rc.d/nginx
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr rc.d 8 ,
.Xr prowld 8 ,
.Xr prowlctl 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
first appeared in MidnightBSD 4.1.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Lucas Holt Aq Mt luke@MidnightBSD.org
